1
00:01:21,530 --> 00:01:24,530
Hello there, Robbie.

2
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:26,530
What are you doing up this late?

3
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:28,530
Reading.

4
00:01:28,530 --> 00:01:29,530
Reading?

5
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:30,530
At this hour?

6
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:31,530
Ah, come on, Robbie.

7
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:32,530
What are you doing up this late?

8
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:35,530
Things on my mind.

9
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:39,530
Do you care to talk about them?

10
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:41,530
Sure,

11
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:43,530
if you don't mind listening.

12
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:46,530
Robbie, Robbie, remember me? Robbie Robbie

13
00:01:46,530 --> 00:01:48,530
I'm your mother.

14
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:51,530
If you have something you want to talk about,

15
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:52,530
I'm always prepared to listen.

16
00:01:52,530 --> 00:01:56,530
You haven't been around much lately.

17
00:01:56,530 --> 00:01:59,530
So that's it.

18
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:01,530
OK, let's talk.

19
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:05,530
You and Dad are like ships that pass in the night.

20
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:08,530
Dad works hard, and he works late.

21
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:10,530
You work hard on all your committees,

22
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:12,530
and you work late.

23
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:14,530
I thought you were proud of the work I do.

24
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:15,530
I am, Mom.

25
00:02:15,530 --> 00:02:16,530
Real proud.

26
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:20,530
You are one fantastic mom,

27
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:24,530
but ... but I've been noticing

28
00:02:24,530 --> 00:02:26,530
how little quality time

29
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:29,530
you spend with Dad and me ... and the family.

30
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:35,530
It's a real problem, Robbie.

31
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,530
I know it.

32
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:42,530
I'm concerned.

33
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:44,530
There must be a way

34
00:02:44,530 --> 00:02:47,530
that Dad and you can spend more time together.

35
00:02:47,530 --> 00:02:51,530
Well, we always talk about

36
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:53,530
taking a vacation together--with the family.

37
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:56,530
I think you ought to

38
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:59,530
take a vacation away from the family--alone.

39
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:01,530
Kind of a second honeymoon.

40
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:04,530
It would be wonderful,

41
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:06,530
but our schedules won't allow it.

42
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:08,530
I think I have an idea.

43
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:10,530
You do?

44
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:11,530
Yup.

45
00:03:11,530 --> 00:03:13,530
I think I have an idea

46
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:14,530
that will bring Dad and you

47
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:16,530
together in a more scheduled way.

48
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,530
What is it?

49
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:19,530
Well,

50
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:21,530
you know how Dad is always talking about

51
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:22,530
the kids in the ward

52
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:25,530
and how important it is for them to be paid attention to?

53
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:26,530
Yes.

54
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:27,530
Well ...

55
00:03:27,530 --> 00:03:28,530
and how hard it is

56
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:30,530
because the doctors and nurses are so busy?

57
00:03:30,530 --> 00:03:31,530
Yes.

58
00:03:31,530 --> 00:03:36,530
Well, how would it be if you took some time

59
00:03:36,530 --> 00:03:38,530
to work with Dad towards solving that problem?

60
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:40,530
I don't get it.

61
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:44,530
Like setting up a regular weekly reading program.

62
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:46,530
You and Dad.

63
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:48,530
You and Dr. Philip Stewart--

64
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:51,530
going to the children's ward once or twice a week

65
00:03:51,530 --> 00:03:52,530
and reading to them.

66
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:55,530
Not bad.

67
00:03:55,530 --> 00:03:57,530
Not a bad idea, Robbie.

68
00:03:57,530 --> 00:03:59,530
As a matter of fact,

69
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:01,530
it fits right in with something I'm working on right now

70
00:04:01,530 --> 00:04:03,530
with the school-board committee.

71
00:04:03,530 --> 00:04:04,530
What's that?

72
00:04:04,530 --> 00:04:06,530
I've been trying

73
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:08,530
to work out a program

74
00:04:08,530 --> 00:04:09,530
in the public school

75
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:13,530
that will bring parents and teachers together once a week

76
00:04:13,530 --> 00:04:16,530
to read to the students--their own children, really.

77
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:18,530
By doing that, it will encourage reading.

78
00:04:18,530 --> 00:04:21,530
So it might fit in with a program

79
00:04:21,530 --> 00:04:23,530
for reading to the kids in the hospital.

80
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:24,530
You're right.

81
00:04:24,530 --> 00:04:26,530
We'll do it!

82
00:04:26,530 --> 00:04:28,530
I'm going to talk to Daddy about it right now.

83
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:32,530
But Dad was so exhausted when he came home from work.

84
00:04:32,530 --> 00:04:34,530
Why don't you talk to him about it tomorrow?

85
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:38,530
You are a very smart young man, Robbie.

86
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:41,530
I think I'll wait until tomorrow.

87
00:04:41,530 --> 00:04:43,530
You won't forget, will you?

88
00:04:43,530 --> 00:04:45,530
Believe me, I won't.

89
00:04:45,530 --> 00:04:47,530
It is a great idea,

90
00:04:47,530 --> 00:04:49,530
and I promise you I won't forget.

91
00:04:49,530 --> 00:04:51,530
Thanks, Mom.

92
00:04:51,530 --> 00:04:54,530
Thank you, Robbie.
